  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 208 PM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nIn the wake of the upper-level low pressure system that will exit to \nthe east by Tuesday evening, broad-scale ridging should set up for \nWednesday across the Desert Southwest with larger scale troughing \nover the Upper Midwest.  This should place west central Texas in \nnorthwest flow aloft and help to push a weak cold front through the \nregion on Wednesday. No rain is expected with this front and high \ntemperatures should reach the mid 70s with just a minor wind shift \nout of the northwest.  The ridge will continue to build in for \nThursday and Friday which should allow high temperatures to reach\nthe upper 70s under sunny skies. Looking ahead to the weekend, \nglobal models are in fairly good agreement on another southern-\nstream system moving through the Four Corners region and into west\nTexas Saturday night through Sunday. This would bring another \nround of Pacific-based moisture into the region for this weekend. \nLow to medium (20-40%) rain chances are currently in the forecast,\nbut track, timing and moisture values will all play a role in how\nmuch rainfall occurs.",
